    "Noise emitted from the air source heat pump shall be controlled such that either:\r\na) the rating level of operational noise, when assessed in accordance with BS 4142:2014+A1:2019, is at least 5 dB below the representative background sound level (LA90,T) at the nearest noise sensitive receptor; or\r\nb) the equipment complies with the permitted development noise standard for air source heat pumps, demonstrated using an MCERTS certified noise assessment methodology.\r\n\r\nThe equipment shall not be brought into use until a post installation noise assessment demonstrating compliance with either of the above criteria has been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The equipment shall thereafter be operated and maintained in accordance with the approved details for the lifetime of the development.\r\n\r\nReason - to protect the amenity of surrounding occupiers"
